                <head>239. Editorial note</head>
                <p>On November 16, 1976, the Ford Administration approved the grant of $400,000 in
                    communications equipment and training for the Government of Sudan. The Sudanese
                    Government had requested the grant for equipment and training to combat
                    terrorism, counter foreign plots against the country, and improve its
                    international communications abilities. The proposal was considered by the
                    Operations Advisory Group on November 8, which unanimously recommended it to
                    President Ford, who signed the finding. (Scowcroft to Ford, November 16;
                    National Security Council, Ford Administration Intelligence Files, Subject
                    Files, Box 13, Sudan)</p>
            </div>
